; `;@axiom:isr(fault)` binds the fault hook. The runtime calls it with
; five `Int`s - the status the fixed exit would answer, the vector
; offset, ESR_EL1, ELR_EL1 and FAR_EL1 - and its `Int` answer is the
; exit status. The call passes five words whatever the declaration
; says, so a declaration that says anything else contradicts the tag:
; AX3010 (axtag-mismatch), at the declaration.
;
; `tooFew` takes two parameters and `wrongType` takes a `String` first.
; `hook` is the control: the declared shape checks clean.
(:: tooFew (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:isr(fault)
(fn (tooFew status vector)
  status)

(:: wrongType (-> String Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:isr(fault)
(fn (wrongType status vector esr elr far)
  vector)

(:: hook (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:isr(fault)
(fn (hook status vector esr elr far)
  status)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  0)
